    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d711-a1">

                <pb facs="0651" n="535" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg535"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ministry for Foreign Affairs to the American
                        Embassy</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sublime Porte</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 15, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Imperial Ministry for Foreign Affairs is informed that the Haitian Government
                    raises great difficulties in the matter of the renewal of licenses to retail
                    merchants of foreign, and particularly of Ottoman, nationality.</p>
                <p>As the Representative of the French Republic has already taken steps towards
                    removing these difficulties, the Imperial Ministry will be obliged to the
                    Embassy of the United States of America if it will kindly use its good offices
                    with its Government to the end that the Representative of the United States in
                    Haiti may be invited to join in these steps.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
